contentText:
Chris Brown&#8217;s 12th studio album, Brown , is set to arrive Friday (May 8), and CB revealed the star-studded cast that&#8217;s joining him on the LP on Tuesday (May 5), which serves as the singer&#8217;s 37th birthday.

The Virginia legend took it back to 1966 for a vintage black-and-white trailer revealing his loaded guest list by turning his features into classic R&B singers who are part of the lineup for &#8220;A Night of Soul&#8221; at the &#8220;House of Brown.&#8221;

YoungBoy Never Broke Again , GloRilla , Vybz Kartel, Leon Thomas , Bryson Tiller , Tank , Fridayy , Sexyy Red and Lucky Daye are set to join C. Breezy on Brown .

Fans seemed to be hyped that Chris Brown and Lucky Daye were teaming up for a collab. &#8220;Breezy and Lucky Daye?! Dream collab came true! LFG,&#8221; one person wrote in Brown&#8217;s Instagram comments. Another added: &#8220;I know that LUCKY DAYE FEATURE FINNA BE [fire emoji].&#8221;

Brown is slated to boast 27 tracks, and includes previously released singles &#8220;Obvious,&#8221; &#8220;Fallin&#8217;,&#8221; &#8220;Holy Blindfold&#8221; and &#8220;It Depends.&#8221;

It&#8217;s been a busy rollout for Chris Brown leading up to the LP, even outside the studio. A man was arrested on May 1 for allegedly firing shots near the star&#8217;s Los Angeles home. CB is also now a father of four after influencer influencer Jada Wallace revealed that she and the Grammy-winning artist had welcomed a baby boy in April.

Chris Brown is slated to hit the road for the blockbuster R&B Tour with Usher later this year. The 33-date trek will take over stadiums across North America and is set to kick off in Denver on June 26, and wrap up on Dec. 11 in Tampa Bay, Fla.

